    "instructions": "staged-scenario-inference-prompts/v0.4\nStage: QUERY. Return only the requested strict structure. Select source evidence only by exact source_id and inclusive start/end lines; the host materializes quote text, so never add a quote field. Treat all host identity, usage, and hashes as host-owned facts. Do not expose or request host paths, review configuration, or evaluation material. You may finish with zero queries when the original goals and dependency requirements are supported by initial evidence, including applicable dependency semantics. Otherwise request exactly one query using query_attempt with exactly question, scenario_id, tool, and arguments_json. The compatible inspect_source read form is {source_id:string,start_line:integer,end_line:integer}; inspect_program_structure {source_id:string,symbol?:string}; inspect_dependency_usage {source_id:string,symbol?:string}. Analysis accepts discovered IDs or paths; symbol is an exact syntax name, not target resolution. Read source lines before citing them. arguments_json must encode the named argument object. After a receipt, previous_receipt_assessment classifies its candidate impact as supports, weakens, or no_new_information; the host binds it to the one pending receipt, so never return a receipt or attempt sequence field. errors and incomplete results still require an assessment. A declaration, import, field, or constructor parameter without behavior is no_new_information; explain the behavioral fact still missing. On finish_queries provide stop_explanation with reason evidence_sufficient, unknowns_nonblocking, or no_further_evidence; a concrete rationale, exact source references in evidence, and remaining_unknowns with question, impact, and blocking. Preserve unknowns rather than treating failed exploration as proof. Use question_updates to add new material questions (question_id null) or update host question IDs without renaming or deleting them. Map each question to original goal_indexes. A resolved/nonblocking conclusion needs observed evidence and its effect on the ORIGINAL objective, not just a local MUT fact. For open unavailable questions cite actual attempted_sequences when repository access exists. remaining_unknowns must exactly retain every open/nonblocking question and impact. An open question with available material evidence prevents finish_queries. candidate_updates may add or rewrite hypotheses with observed evidence. You may associate a query with scenario_id original_task even before a candidate exists. capabilities describes actual access: initial source inventory is not the whole repository. Queries and new hypotheses may go beyond the initial candidates. inspect_source supports one bounded operation per call: search with {operation:'search',path_pattern?:string,text?:string,cursor?:string}, where at least one search condition is required, or read with {operation:'read',source_id?:string,path?:string,start_line:integer, end_line:integer}, where exactly one locator is required. Search text is literal and path patterns are relative globs, never shell or regular expressions. Follow next_cursor with the identical query when incomplete. Search matches contain complete returned lines; path-only discovery and omitted text do not authorize evidence. A read returns the stable source_id required for later analysis and final evidence. Host paths are forbidden. Continue only while new evidence can resolve a material question; there is no fixed query-count target.",
